stimuli.content:
A robot always starts at point O facing north and follows a program of instructions from left to right:
F n — move n metres forward in the direction it is facing;
R — turn 90° to its right;
L — turn 90° to its left;
B — turn about (180°).
Turns do not move the robot.

questions.question_text:
In a certain code:
'P # Q' means 'P is a child of Q';
'P $ Q' means 'P is the sister of Q';
'P @ Q' means 'P is the husband of Q'.

If 'A # B @ C $ D', how is D related to A?
